 "char": {
  "id": "dave2",
  "handle": "deep_water_dave",
  "name": "Dave",
  "bio": "Twenty years in salvage. Ask me about the sea floor.",
  "voice": "am_onyx",
  "case": "maryceleste",
  "look": {
   "skin": "#d8a882",
   "hair": "#6b6b6b",
   "style": "bald",
   "shirt": "#24394f",
   "glasses": false,
   "extra": "mask"
  },
  "script": "In salvage, you learn that ships tell you things. December 1872. The Mary Celeste is found drifting in the Atlantic, sails up, nobody aboard. Six months of food. Her cargo of alcohol almost untouched. One lifeboat gone. The captain, his wife, their two-year-old daughter and seven crew were never seen again. My guess? Something scared them into that boat, and the ship sailed on without them. But honestly, nobody knows."
 },
